Error: Jet.DispatchHoleCount: An `if` table header holds one `<>` hole, and this one has 2
  --> Tests/UI/e0946_dispatch_hole_twice.jet:4:8
    |
  4 |     if n % <> == <> {
    |        ^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: Each arm's candidate takes the place of the one `<>`, so a second `<>` would stand for nothing
 Fix: Keep one `<>` and write the other value out in the header
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.DispatchHoleCount
